    "title": "City Bikes",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "In our city, you can rent a bike at more than thirty stations. The bikes are blue and easy to ride. Many tourists and local people use them every day."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "To rent a bike, you need a card or a phone app. Go to a station, choose a bike, and ride! It costs one pound for the first thirty minutes. After that, it costs two pounds an hour. You can leave the bike at any station in the city."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "The bikes have a basket at the front and a light at the back. Helmets are not free, so bring your own. There are special bike roads in the city centre and along the river. They are safe, and cars cannot go on them."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "The bike rental is open from six in the morning to eleven at night. In winter, fewer people use the bikes because it is cold and dark. The city has a plan to buy five hundred new bikes next year, and to open ten new stations near the schools."
      }
    ]
  },
